cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Grand canonical Monte Carlo of CO2 in rigid large-pore MIL-53(Al):
  validation of a GCMC workflow against experiment
message: "If you use this workflow or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ariskina
    given-names: Kristina
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5782-2222"
    city: Pau
    country: FR
abstract: >-
  A grand canonical Monte Carlo workflow (RASPA2) for CO2 adsorption in the
  large-pore form of MIL-53(Al) at 304 K, validated against RASPA's own reference
  calculations, against the manometric isotherm of Bourrelly et al. (2005) and
  against the osmotic-ensemble analysis of Coudert et al. (2008), with a
  cross-code check against LAMMPS fix gcmc. The rigid framework reproduces the
  saturation capacity of the open form to 0.5 %, while the generic UFF/DDEC/TraPPE
  force field gives a Langmuir constant 3.95 times too high, i.e. it over-binds
  CO2 at low coverage.
keywords:
  - grand canonical Monte Carlo
  - GCMC
  - MIL-53
  - metal-organic framework
  - CO2 adsorption
  - RASPA
  - LAMMPS
  - molecular simulation
